id: pm-pwq0g5
title: "The public harness detectors default env to an empty object, so detectAgentIdentity() and detectHarnessIdentity() silently return empty for every SDK caller"
description: "src/core/shared/author.ts:438 reads 'const env = signals.env ?? {}', so the two public detectors evaluate every descriptor against a zero-key environment when called with no arguments. Verified live: CLAUDECODE=1 is set and detectAgentIdentity() still returns {}. The CLI is unaffected because resolveAuthorIdentity routes through effectiveHarnessDetectionSignals, which supplies process.env."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",extensibility,identity,silent-failure
created_at: "2026-07-26T18:25:57.996Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T06:26:35.854Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T06:23:16.252Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "detectAgentIdentity() called with no arguments inside a known harness returns that harness rather than an empty object; The injected-signals path used by tests continues to work unchanged, including the AsyncLocalStorage seam; detectAgentIdentity and detectHarnessIdentity are documented in docs/SDK.md with the environment-resolution contract stated explicitly"
goal: project management = context management
value: "Makes automatic identity detection actually reachable from the SDK, which is the precondition for packages that adapt behaviour per harness."
impact: "Any package gating on harness identity degrades to its no-harness branch on every host with no error, no warning, and no telemetry."
outcome: "The public detectors resolve the ambient environment by default, or require the parameter so omission is a compile error; the symbols are documented in docs/SDK.md."
why_now: "Harness identity is the seam the project is actively investing in, and the one entry point an extension author would call is the one that cannot work."
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Public no-argument identity detectors now consume ambient environment, argv, and registered client signals while preserving explicit injectable inputs for deterministic callers."
expected_result: detectAgentIdentity() and detectHarnessIdentity() identify supported harnesses without callers forwarding process state.
actual_result: "Ambient Codex detection and installed Node/Bun consumers return the harness plus bounded model, effort, role, session, and privacy-safe instance provenance."
